    "show_share": true,
    "description": "When Minza Muhandagani, an educator and health professional from Chalinze District Council, Tanzania, boarded a plane to the United Kingdom in July 2024, she was embarking on what would become a life-changing journey. Supported by the Aga Khan University's Institute for Educational Development, East Africa (IED, EA), Minza joined the prestigious University of Cambridge Summer Programme. This four-week experience brought together learners from across the world to explore new ideas, challenge perspectives, and build bridges between disciplines.",
